314
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:43,640
"I'm sorry.

315
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,480
Of course, on the one hand...

316
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:51,400
But on the other hand...
On the one hand, I don't want to,

317
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,400
but on the other hand,
if I don't...".

318
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:56,200
So, I'm always
in the "On the one hand, on the other hand,

319
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:59,720
on the other hand, on the other hand,
I'm sorry, I'm afraid to disappoint."

320
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:01,960
And with all this story I don't define myself

321
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,160
and, since I don't define myself,
the rest defines me,

322
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,280
and the rest does what they want with us.

323
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:10,960
So, here, we're taking it,
we're holding on, we're holding on.

324
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:15,240
And, after so much patience,
comes the fourth and final point, Reyes.

325
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:19,040
We finally arrive at the fourth point.

326
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:23,960
Repressed anger.

327
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,560
What's happening?

328
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:28,600
After so much holding on, keeping quiet, keeping quiet, holding

329
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,720
on, holding on, holding on, there

330
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,800
comes a day when I can't take it anymore.

331
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,440
Why?

332
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:37,480
Because I've been repressing the discomforts, I've

333
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,880
been repressing the injustices, I've

334
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:42,440
been repressing
the desire I had to...

335
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:44,800
But no, no,
behave yourself, behave yourself, behave yourself.

336
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:49,160
No, it's my duty, it's my duty.

337
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,560
But there comes a day when you can't take it anymore.

338
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,080
And has it never happened to you

339
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,440
that there is a day
when you can't take it anymore and you just give up?  Has it

340
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:01,600
ever happened to you
that there comes a day when you have to do the math?

341
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:08,160
And, when you've done the trick,
doesn't it occur to you that your friends,

342
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:11,880
the people close to you, look at you and say:
"But what happened to you? It's

343
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,600
not that big of a deal.

344
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,080
But it's just stupid"?

345
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,720
But what happens?

346
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:21,800
When you've let off steam

347
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:25,120
and everyone has looked at you
with a "poor" face, "poor",

348
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,280
then you feel guilty.

349
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,920
Then, you realize you've gone too far.

350
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,760
And what are you doing?

351
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,760
Once again inside.  You

352
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,800
know that "behave yourself,

353
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,160
do what they expect you to do

354
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:43,440
because if you don't, they won't like you."

355
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:47,360
Imagine having before you a young girl,

356
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:50,600
30 years old,
of extraordinary beauty,

357
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,960
who, apart from telling me
that she already considered herself old,

358
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,360
on the other hand,

359
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,760
tells you: "When I am me, I don't like it.

360
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:05,680
On the other hand, when I am what they expect,
then I like it."

361
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,880
So, how is my life?

362
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:10,000
Always do what others like.

363
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,160
Oysters!

364
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:16,000
I hope I have given you key clues

365
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,680
and that, from here on, you

366
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:21,560
can rethink a little what we
call bad kindness.

367
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:34,240
Hello, Xavier.
It's a pleasure to be here with you.

368
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:35,920
-Likewise.
-My name is Miguel

369
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,560
and I am now worried
about my children's education.

370
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,680
I want them to be good, to
be obedient,

371
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:45,720
but I'm afraid they'll be do-gooders,

372
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:47,200
that they'll say "yes" to everything.

373
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:50,080
What could you advise me
to avoid this error?

374
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:53,120
Advising on education
is impossible.

375
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,520
Impossible, I don't dare.

376
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:02,440
Normally, we
tend to do what has been done to us,

377
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:06,440
therefore, even if we give advice

378
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:10,200
and want to give magic formulas,

379
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:13,680
in the end,
parents get what they have learned

380
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:16,200
and repeat the same
with their children.

381
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:20,360
Therefore, it is a joint learning,

382
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,240
children and parents learn continuously.

383
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:24,880
But, well, let's get to your question.

384
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:29,440
I remember a training session

385
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,720
and, before the training started,

386
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:33,440
I went out to have breakfast.

387
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:37,720
At breakfast I
had a family in front of me.

388
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,320
Father, mother and a little girl,

389
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:43,320
I would say she was
between 6 and 8 years old, no more.

390
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,400
They made my breakfast bitter,

391
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:49,840
especially my mother.  It

392
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,520
could have been the father,

393
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:54,480
in another situation it
would have been the father.

394
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:55,800
In this case, it was the mother.

395
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,320
The 20 minutes

396
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:03,800
meant that every minute
this girl received an order.

397
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,200
"Sit still,

398
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,400
don't stand up, don't cross your legs,

399
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,800
now don't touch this,
pick this up with your fork."

400
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,680
They were continuous orders.

401
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:15,560
Obviously, we can't say,
"Children shouldn't be educated."

402
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:16,720
Man, of course.

403
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,760
Obviously, they have to learn limits, they

404
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,080
have to learn options, they

405
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,080
have to learn what can be,
what can't be.  Obviously.

406
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:26,840
In this sense,
if you are an educational parent,

407
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:29,960
especially if you are a provider parent,

408
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,600
great.

409
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:35,200
Even better
if you are a facilitating parent.  A

410
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:37,440
providing father is one who
gives you what you need.  A

411
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:42,320
facilitating parent is someone who makes it
easier for you to talk,

412
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,520
play together, etc.

413
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,680
Good.  The

414
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:49,160
only thing I dare to say is:

415
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,920
Plato,

416
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,520
when he
talks about education,

417
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:58,520
leaves us with a message that is,
for me, fundamental.

418
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,880
"Educating is bringing out from within."

419
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:04,080
What does it mean?

420
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:08,600
That this child,
the parents, are skilled enough,

421
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,320
curious and attentive

422
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:15,480
to what is coming out of their child.

423
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:20,680
Where he leans,
what he likes, what he wants to try,

424
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,920
what things catch his attention.

425
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:27,720
Anyone who has more than one child realizes that one wants
one thing and the other wants another.

426
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,520
Even if you educate them the same.

427
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:32,000
Therefore, there
is something they carry inside,

428
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:37,240
and this is where we make a mistake if we want to see
children as a blank slate.

429
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:41,280
Children are like a blank sheet of paper
that needs to be molded,

430
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:44,000
that needs to be recreated,

431
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:47,680
and parents are the ones who need to
mold this slate

432
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:48,760
and write.

433
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,760
No, no, no.

434
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:52,240
Children are not a blank slate, they

435
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:55,720
already carry a lot of information.

436
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:59,560
And this information unfolds

437
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:02,080
as they live
and encounter situations.

438
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:05,400
Parents must be careful.

439
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,880
Therefore, the only thing
I dare to say to you, Miguel, is:

440
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,200
