in their own image and likeness.  We

452
00:22:57,240 --> 00:23:02,080
don't want to mold our children too much,

453
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:07,480
but rather accompany them,
better bring them out from within.

454
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:09,360
And how do I get them out?

455
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:12,120
Partly, by observing where they lean,

456
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:14,160
partly, by asking them questions,

457
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:18,680
partly, by asking them
why they like this,

458
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:20,080
why they don't like that.

459
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:23,000
And don't give him a clue, no:
"You must like it",

460
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,200
"But that's silly"...

461
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,160
And you have to take it into account,

462
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:28,680
not punish him, not take him out of it,

463
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,080
but accompany him

464
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:35,320
and discover where it's taking him
and to what extent you need to intervene,

465
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,880
but simply to give him clues

466
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:41,760
so that he can rethink what he's
going through.  I believe

467
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:47,000
this task
is impossible today

468
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:50,960
because we live
in a culture of performance

469
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:52,760
where there is no time for anything.

470
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:54,840
Then, we immediately put them

471
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:57,360
in the dynamics of rush,
performance, we

472
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:59,600
put them in our culture.

473
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:02,720
That's why
I believe that being a parent today

474
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,960
takes incredible courage.

475
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:08,320
Incredible.

476
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,000
With enormous courage.  I'm

477
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:12,480
